2026-09-27T12:05:55.0956617Z This PPA contains more recent Python versions packaged for Ubuntu.
2026-09-27T12:05:55.0956965Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:55.0957791Z Disclaimer: there's no guarantee of timely updates in case of security problems or other issues. If you want to use them in a security-or-otherwise-critical environment (say, on a production server), you do so at your own risk.
2026-09-27T12:05:55.0958736Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:55.0958821Z Update Note
2026-09-27T12:05:55.0959039Z ===========
2026-09-27T12:05:55.0959346Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T12:05:55.0959620Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:55.0959713Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T12:05:55.0959929Z ================
2026-09-27T12:05:55.0960054Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:55.0960291Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T12:05:55.0960817Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T12:05:55.0961054Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:55.0961165Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T12:05:55.0961458Z ====================================
2026-09-27T12:05:55.0961655Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:55.0961798Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T12:05:55.0962178Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T12:05:55.0962546Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T12:05:55.0963253Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T12:05:55.0963840Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:55.0963949Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T12:05:55.0964392Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T12:05:55.0964990Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T12:05:55.0965304Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:55.0965634Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T12:05:55.0966095Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:55.0966186Z Packages
2026-09-27T12:05:55.0966372Z ========
2026-09-27T12:05:55.0966480Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:55.0967912Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T12:05:55.0969382Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:55.0969643Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T12:05:55.0970193Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T12:05:55.0971268Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T12:05:55.0971959Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T12:05:55.0972601Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T12:05:55.1043479Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T12:05:55.1044291Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:55.1044462Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T12:05:55.1044748Z ==========================
2026-09-27T12:05:55.1044935Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:55.1046169Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T12:05:55.1047437Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:55.1048104Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T12:05:55.1049080Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T12:05:55.1049297Z 
